WEBVTT

00:00:00.676 --> 00:00:01.630
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.978 --> 00:00:04.270
In this lesson, we do two styles:

00:00:04.459 --> 00:00:06.670
a classic side part, and then a crop.

00:00:07.023 --> 00:00:10.398
The preparation, the neck strip, and washing your hands,

00:00:10.348 --> 00:00:13.070
you do as in the men's haircut basics lesson.

00:00:13.493 --> 00:00:16.030
You heard the reason for each step in the theory lesson.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.310
Here, we do it.

00:00:17.855 --> 00:00:18.609
Step one:

00:00:18.902 --> 00:00:22.369
the consultation to choose the style, while the hair is still dry.

00:00:23.034 --> 00:00:24.689
Ask to see a reference photo.

00:00:24.939 --> 00:00:27.466
Look at the face, at the density at the front,

00:00:27.416 --> 00:00:29.889
and look for a cowlick at the front hairline.

00:00:30.398 --> 00:00:33.549
Ask how many minutes the client has for his hair each morning,

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:34.849
and whether he blow-dries.

00:00:35.195 --> 00:00:36.769
Agree on both parts together:

00:00:36.959 --> 00:00:39.969
the sides, taper or fade, and how high;

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:43.569
the top, how much to leave, and how long at the front.

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:45.186
The side part.

00:00:45.436 --> 00:00:46.226
Step two:

00:00:46.405 --> 00:00:47.826
find the natural parting.

00:00:48.227 --> 00:00:50.866
Wet the hair evenly, and comb it all back.

00:00:51.275 --> 00:00:53.666
Push the top gently forward with your palm.

00:00:54.011 --> 00:00:56.866
Where the hair separates, that is the natural parting.

00:00:57.212 --> 00:00:59.586
Redraw it cleanly with the tail of the comb.

00:01:00.078 --> 00:01:03.586
If the client wants the parting on the other side, tell him beforehand:

00:01:03.928 --> 00:01:07.826
the hair may not lie flat, and will need more careful blow-drying every morning.

00:01:08.498 --> 00:01:09.274
Step three:

00:01:09.511 --> 00:01:10.234
the sides.

00:01:10.784 --> 00:01:15.674
Taper or fade, as agreed, as in the fade lesson and the men's haircut basics lesson.

00:01:16.183 --> 00:01:18.474
A taper is subtle, and suits the office.

00:01:18.822 --> 00:01:20.794
A fade looks younger and sharper.

00:01:21.279 --> 00:01:23.931
On the parting side, don't take the sides too high,

00:01:23.881 --> 00:01:26.074
so the parting still has somewhere to sit.

00:01:26.704 --> 00:01:27.513
Step four:

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:28.313
the top.

00:01:28.896 --> 00:01:32.953
Take the first section at the crown, lift it, and cut the agreed length.

00:01:33.208 --> 00:01:34.233
This is your guideline.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.808
Then work gradually toward the forehead,

00:01:36.758 --> 00:01:39.273
pulling each section back toward the guideline.

00:01:39.782 --> 00:01:43.513
Over-directing like this makes the hair gradually longer toward the front.

00:01:43.862 --> 00:01:47.188
The front is the longest, so when it is combed to the side,

00:01:47.138 --> 00:01:49.353
the hair falls nicely over the parting.

00:01:49.687 --> 00:01:50.233
Remember:

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:54.953
long can always be cut shorter, but once it is short, it can't be undone.

00:01:55.356 --> 00:01:59.186
Comb the hair over along the parting to test it, see whether it falls well,

00:01:59.136 --> 00:02:02.713
and check in the mirror that both sides of the forehead look balanced.

00:02:03.378 --> 00:02:04.249
Step five:

00:02:04.432 --> 00:02:05.209
point cutting.

00:02:05.732 --> 00:02:09.829
Take each section, point the tips of the scissors straight into the ends,

00:02:09.779 --> 00:02:11.049
and cut small notches.

00:02:11.317 --> 00:02:14.089
The ends soften, with no hard cutting line.

00:02:14.587 --> 00:02:16.249
For fine hair, go lightly.

00:02:16.598 --> 00:02:18.409
For thick hair, you can cut deeper.

00:02:18.889 --> 00:02:21.449
Don't texturize close to the roots along the parting:

00:02:21.711 --> 00:02:23.209
the short hairs will stand up.

00:02:23.444 --> 00:02:25.542
Then check it in the opposite direction,

00:02:25.492 --> 00:02:28.409
and blend the top into the sides with scissor over comb.

00:02:29.053 --> 00:02:31.373
Step six, only if the client wants it:

00:02:31.558 --> 00:02:32.493
a hard part.

00:02:32.908 --> 00:02:35.293
This is a thin line shaved along the parting.

00:02:35.802 --> 00:02:37.213
Tell the client beforehand:

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:41.628
with a hard part, you can't switch sides anymore, and when it grows back,

00:02:41.578 --> 00:02:43.133
it looks fuzzy for a while.

00:02:43.564 --> 00:02:46.413
Fit a new, single-use blade in the razor.

00:02:46.682 --> 00:02:51.100
Stretch the skin, hold the blade almost flat against the skin,

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.213
and shave a thin line, slowly.

00:02:53.637 --> 00:02:55.213
Don't go too far into the top.

00:02:55.864 --> 00:02:56.741
Step seven:

00:02:56.967 --> 00:02:57.701
blow-dry.

00:02:58.118 --> 00:03:00.821
Dry the roots first, in the direction of the style:

00:03:01.009 --> 00:03:02.981
from the parting over to the other side.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.901
Lift the roots at the front gently with your fingers, for volume.

00:03:07.427 --> 00:03:09.781
Once the roots are dry, the shape holds.

00:03:10.209 --> 00:03:13.221
Finally, give it a little cool air to set the shape.

00:03:13.607 --> 00:03:15.846
Keep the dryer some distance from the head,

00:03:15.796 --> 00:03:18.341
and don't let the heat blow on one spot for long.

00:03:18.979 --> 00:03:19.705
Step eight:

00:03:19.851 --> 00:03:20.505
product.

00:03:20.817 --> 00:03:22.905
Pomade for a shiny, neat look;

00:03:23.174 --> 00:03:25.065
matte wax for a more natural look.

00:03:25.411 --> 00:03:30.106
Just a little, rubbed evenly between your palms, worked through from back to front,

00:03:30.056 --> 00:03:31.785
then combed along the parting.

00:03:32.127 --> 00:03:36.345
Show the client how to redo it at home, then hold up a hand mirror so he can see.

00:03:36.953 --> 00:03:38.989
Now the crop, on a different client.

00:03:39.309 --> 00:03:40.189
Step nine:

00:03:40.436 --> 00:03:41.229
the sides.

00:03:41.578 --> 00:03:44.988
Usually a low or mid fade, done as in the fade lesson.

00:03:45.419 --> 00:03:47.933
Blend the fade into the top really smoothly,

00:03:47.883 --> 00:03:51.629
because a crop has no long hair falling over it to hide the blend.

00:03:52.186 --> 00:03:53.078
Step ten:

00:03:53.253 --> 00:03:54.198
the short top.

00:03:54.592 --> 00:03:59.158
Lift each section, and cut the agreed length, evenly from the crown to the front.

00:03:59.592 --> 00:04:04.457
Then point cut more, and deeper than for the side part, so the top has texture,

00:04:04.407 --> 00:04:05.798
with separated pieces.

00:04:06.423 --> 00:04:07.321
Step eleven:

00:04:07.556 --> 00:04:08.681
the fringe line.

00:04:09.005 --> 00:04:10.841
Comb the fringe straight forward.

00:04:11.102 --> 00:04:14.896
Hold it between two fingers, and cut a short line, at the agreed height,

00:04:14.846 --> 00:04:17.081
usually around the middle of the forehead.

00:04:17.658 --> 00:04:20.601
Ask the client to close his eyes while you cut the fringe.

00:04:21.023 --> 00:04:25.001
The scissor blade always stays below your fingers, never touching the skin.

00:04:25.339 --> 00:04:28.985
Look straight into the mirror, and check that the fringe line is even,

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:29.961
from left to right.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:33.306
Then point cut lightly along the line to soften it,

00:04:33.256 --> 00:04:35.801
unless the client wants a really straight line.

00:04:36.388 --> 00:04:39.480
If the client has a strong cowlick at the front hairline,

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:41.241
leave the fringe a little longer,

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:43.001
so it is heavy enough to lie down.

00:04:43.663 --> 00:04:44.605
Step twelve:

00:04:44.713 --> 00:04:45.485
styling.

00:04:45.971 --> 00:04:49.645
You can blow-dry first, using your fingers to push the hair forward.

00:04:50.146 --> 00:04:53.701
For fine hair, spray a little sea salt spray before drying,

00:04:53.651 --> 00:04:55.245
so the hair looks thicker.

00:04:55.822 --> 00:05:00.925
Once the hair is dry, take a little matte wax, and rub it evenly between your hands.

00:05:01.274 --> 00:05:05.245
Scrunch the top, twist each piece lightly, and push it forward.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.205
Don't comb it.

00:05:06.389 --> 00:05:09.405
A crop looks best when it looks a bit natural and textured.

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:13.965
Hand the client the wax so he can try it once, then hold up a hand mirror for him.

00:05:14.556 --> 00:05:17.006
Before the client leaves, write it in the record:

00:05:17.294 --> 00:05:21.957
which style, which side the parting is on, how the sides were done,

00:05:21.907 --> 00:05:24.366
how long the top is, which product.

00:05:24.881 --> 00:05:27.966
Book the next visit, usually in about three to five weeks.

00:05:28.287 --> 00:05:32.603
Tools are cleaned and disinfected, and razor blades go into the sharps container,

00:05:32.553 --> 00:05:34.446
as in the lesson on cleaning tools.

00:05:34.795 --> 00:05:37.566
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
